this is a continuation of:

https://github.com/bahamas10/bash-md5
https://github.com/bahamas10/c-md5

thought it would be fun to dive into the rabbit hole directly.

first modified (C version) to match (within 2-5%) `md5sum` from `coreutils`

then ASM optis (using unwind tables) based on gcc `-O3` analysis => asm translations.

using `objdump` and `perf` mostly and stealing from `libcrypto`.

finally, write a generator for testing changes in a simpler language.

===

#   ./gen_asm.py > md5.s
#   as md5.s -o md5.o && ld md5.o -o md5
#   ./test-md5

completes a 1GB file, single stream, in about 1 second (Intel i5-1345U @ 4.70).
